{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact head 9adfe7a03de24483518744f15fadb71368ea7050 on builder/u1-upgrade-application-20261117, all 44 artifacts, for request 834f24c7 under my promise 4497393c. The implementation is U1 (request ea7faed9, promise 07c54062). The reporting artifact is the U1 note.\n\nOne finding blocks: two in-place upgrades of one item can run at once, and the later outcome wins, whichever release it carries. The rest of the head is sound.\n\n## The finding\n\n`application-upgrade-proof` refuses `application-upgrade-pending` only when `pendingSuccessor` finds a pending installation item with `replaces` = N (`upgrade-rules.ts`, `pendingSuccessor`). The in-place form opens no item. It opens only a `fetch-application` operation and changes N at the confirmed outcome. Nothing records the open in-place fetch, so the guard cannot see it.\n\nFailure: N is at release R1. A member files `upgrade-application` in place to R2, then a second one to R3, before the first outcome. Both pass the guard, because each release differs from R1 and no successor item exists. Both fetch operations open. The `derives` of `application-fetch` writes `uri`, `release` and `presentation` from whichever confirmed outcome arrives last. If the R3 fetch confirms first (for example, the R2 fetch answers `unknown` and the host retries it), N ends at R2, the older release, and nothing records that R3 was dropped. The same holds for any two in-place acts, and for an in-place act filed after a replace act's successor has been refused.\n\nRuling 8f26aa9b settles D3 (\"never two active, never none\") for the replace form. It does not rule on concurrent in-place acts, and neither the approved note nor the U1 note mentions them. The tests cover a second act only while a replace successor is pending (red (d), line 67-68).\n\nRequired: refuse `application-upgrade-pending` while an in-place fetch of N is open, the same refusal the replace form uses. If the rules state cannot answer \"an open fetch operation of an `upgrade-application` act on N\" cheaply, say so in the note and propose the smallest record that can, for example a changeable reference on N to the open act. Add a test: two in-place acts on N, where the second refuses `application-upgrade-pending` until the first outcome. Add a red that breaks the new check. The gate needs to run again at the new head.\n\n## A question for the planner, not blocking\n\nThe guard refuses an equal release but accepts any other release from the same publisher with the same semantic identifier, including an older one. The trust list still bounds it: a release outside `APPLICATION_TRUST` refuses at the host. If the planner wants in-place upgrades to move forward only, that needs a version order in the signed manifest, and the planner should file it as a separate request. I do not hold U1 for it.\n\n## What I read\n\n- The U1 note, ruling 8f26aa9b, and sections 1, 2 and 4 of the approved upgrade note.\n- `upgrade-rules.ts` in full. The in-place form keys on the equal semantic identifier, and the guard also requires `checked.semantic.entry` to equal N's `definition`. It refuses `roles`, `values` and `owner` in place. `upgradeAnswer` admits a confirmed body only with the act's `uri` and `release` and N's `semantic` and `publisher`, and a refused body only with a known install refusal. A refused or unknown outcome derives nothing, and `holds` and `derives` both require N to be `active`. The replace form opens the successor at the act's own position, pending, with `replaces` = N, and runs the Rules 15 install proof. `application-keep-creation` moves N to `replaced` only in the `created` result entry, and only while N is `active`.\n- The in-place form skips admission and grants. The v2 semantic identifier hashes the roles, capabilities, rights and composition (`application-package-v2.ts`, `semantics`), so an equal identifier keeps the grants. That matches option A of the approved note: \"No scope or grant changes.\"\n- `outside.ts`. The host prepares a fetch for `upgrade-application` exactly as for `install-application`, on attempt 1 of the act's own operation. Red (c) runs the real outside port and shows that the trust check refuses before any source opens.\n- The session fixture fix (`session-room.ts`). Register 29 installs on `github.com`, as the `base` family does. That explains the first END 17c34ab2. It changes no code outside test support.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- The gate. END eb4583bd passed at this head. The first line of `gate.txt` names this head with 0 changed files, and the log ends \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\".\n- The reds. `artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-u1-red/` holds `a.txt`, `b.txt`, `c.txt`, `c2.txt` and `d.txt`. Their SHA-256 values equal the five in the note's table.\n- Scope. The 44 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 83371009 9adfe7a0`. `git merge-tree --write-tree 83371009 9adfe7a0` gives fcfe56b9, the head's tree.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 8 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n- Wake rate. U1 adds no alarm, retry or timed transition. An in-place upgrade costs one act entry, one host fetch and one outcome entry. A replace costs the same as one install. Ruling 8f26aa9b holds deployment until U2, so no rate read follows U1.\n\nArchitecture: sound. A new creation family carries the act, `NEWEST` and every Worker configuration stay on `base`, and each new pin answers the version questions of the pin it follows.\n\nSecurity: one blocking finding, the concurrent in-place race above. The trust check, the publisher check and the in-place field limits hold. The seals moved with the reviewed source, and no signed release changes.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nThis verdict authorizes no push, landing or deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:73b3671fc986389aa23d9df4b1b45167cd04b7c0","binding":"assigned","head":"9adfe7a03de24483518744f15fadb71368ea7050","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4497393c0380f588272142e1df38cecff01df3a0\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:07c54062c0f178ef645a640f0948d0834867183b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4497393c0380f588272142e1df38cecff01df3a0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}